---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import Hero from '../components/Hero.astro';
---

<Layout
  title="Privacy Policy · b-ark-chrome · b-oss"
  description="Privacy policy for b-ark-chrome — the Chrome extension that backs up your Blipfoto journal to a folder on your own device."
  narrow
>
  <Hero label="Privacy hero" title="Privacy Policy — b-ark-chrome">b-ark-chrome is a Chrome browser extension that backs up your Blipfoto journal
      entries and images to a folder on your own device. This policy explains what data
      the extension handles and what happens to it.</Hero>

  <section
    class="block"
    style="border-top: none; padding-top: 0"
    data-screen-label="Privacy body"
  >
    <div class="prose">
      <p><strong>Last updated:</strong> June 2026</p>

      <h2>Who is responsible for this extension</h2>
      <p>
        b-ark-chrome is developed and maintained by Ian Stevenson. Questions about this
        policy can be directed to the contact details in the Chrome Web Store listing.
      </p>

      <h2>What data the extension handles</h2>
      <p>To back up your Blipfoto journal, the extension:</p>
      <ul>
        <li>
          Authenticates you to Blipfoto using OAuth 2.0 and stores the resulting access
          token, encrypted with AES-GCM, in your browser's local extension storage.
        </li>
        <li>
          Fetches your journal entries, metadata, and images from the Blipfoto API and
          its associated content delivery infrastructure.
        </li>
        <li>Writes that content to a local folder on your device that you select.</li>
        <li>
          Stores extension settings and backup status in your browser's local extension
          storage.
        </li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Where your data goes</h2>
      <p>
        Nowhere except your own device. The extension communicates only with Blipfoto's
        own servers (<code>api.blipfoto.com</code> and associated infrastructure) to
        retrieve your content. It does not send your data, your Blipfoto credentials,
        your journal content, or any usage information to the developer or any third
        party. No analytics, crash reporting, or telemetry of any kind is collected.
      </p>

      <h2>What is stored and where</h2>
      <p>
        All extension state (settings, backup status, encrypted token) is held in
        <code>chrome.storage.local</code> on your device. Your access token is stored
        encrypted; the encryption key is held in your browser's IndexedDB and never
        leaves your device. Your backed-up journal content is written to the local folder
        you choose. Nothing is synced to your Google account or any remote storage.
      </p>

      <h2>Blipfoto's own privacy practices</h2>
      <p>
        When you authenticate and when the extension fetches your journal, your requests
        are processed by Blipfoto's servers under Blipfoto's own privacy policy. This
        extension has no control over Blipfoto's data practices.
      </p>

      <h2>Your rights</h2>
      <p>
        Because this extension holds no data about you on any server the developer
        controls, there is nothing for the developer to retrieve, correct, or delete on
        your behalf. All data held by the extension exists on your own device and is under
        your control. You can remove it at any time by uninstalling the extension or
        deleting the backup folder.
      </p>

      <h2>Changes to this policy</h2>
      <p>
        If this policy changes materially, the updated version will be published at this
        URL with a revised date at the top.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>
</Layout>
